Bootstrap: docker-daemon
From: materials-triage:api:latest

# Apptainer recipe beside Compose, for clusters without Docker at run time.
# Build the Docker image first on a machine with Docker, then:
#   apptainer build materials-triage.sif apptainer/materials-triage.def
# Or from a registry copy of the image: change the header to
#   Bootstrap: docker
#   From: <registry>/materials-triage:api
# Written against the Apptainer definition-file reference; not built on the development
# machine (no Apptainer on macOS). The first build on the target cluster is the test.

%environment
    export DATA_CACHE_DIR=${DATA_CACHE_DIR:-$HOME/.materials-triage}
    export AUTH_MODE=${AUTH_MODE:-none}
    export LLM_PROVIDER=${LLM_PROVIDER:-none}
    export FETCH_MODE=${FETCH_MODE:-replay}
    export PATH=/opt/venv/bin:$PATH

%runscript
    # Serves the API and the web app on the port given as the first argument (default 8000).
    # Settings come from the environment or an --env-file; see docs/ADMIN_GUIDE.md.
    PORT="${1:-8000}"
    mkdir -p "$DATA_CACHE_DIR"
    cd /app
    exec materials-triage serve --host 0.0.0.0 --port "$PORT"

%help
    materials-triage: triage candidate materials from public data.
      apptainer run materials-triage.sif [port]
      apptainer run --env-file .env materials-triage.sif 8000
    The image carries the recorded source data; with no keys and no database it answers from
    those. Bind a writable directory to DATA_CACHE_DIR to keep run bundles across runs.
